<title>UK: Venezuelan pumped 2.405 mln bpd in April - OPECNA.</title>
<headline>Venezuelan pumped 2.405 mln bpd in April - OPECNA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC member Venezuela told the group's secretariat it pumped 2.405 million barrels per day (bpd) in April, the OPEC news agency OPECNA said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Venezuela's OPEC quota -- defined by supply to the market rather than wellhead output -- is 2.359 million bpd.</p>
<p>OPEC defines supply as domestic consumption plus net export sales of crude and products plus withdrawls of stocks held outside national boundaries. The supply figure for Venezuela in April was not available, OPECNA said.</p>
<p>A Reuters survey of analysts and industry sources found that Venezuela produced 3.18 million bpd in March.</p>
<p>OPECNA also gave April production figures for Indonesia, Kuwait, Libya and Qatar, detailed below in thousand bpd.</p>
<p> COUNTRY    PRODUCTION     SUPPLY</p>
<p> -------    ----------     ------</p>
<p> INDONESIA  1,327.8	  N.A.</p>
<p> KUWAIT     2,006.8	  N.A.</p>
<p> LIBYA	1,394.0	  N.A.</p>
<p> QATAR	  413.2	  N.A.</p>
<p> VENEZUELA  2,405.0	  N.A.</p>
<p>N.A. - NOT AVAILABLE</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7629</p>
